## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical on-device ML expertise, cross-language support, privacy-preserving inference, and the ability to balance model size with functionality in a realistic chat application.

## Key Concepts
- On-device machine learning and privacy-first design
- Lightweight multilingual models for resource-constrained environments
- Explainability through keyword attribution and contribution scoring
- Offline labeling pipelines and evaluation methodologies

## Code Example
```javascript
function predict(text) {
  const keywords = extractKeywords(text);
  const embeddings = model.embed(keywords);
  const intent = classifier.predict(embeddings);
  const tone = sentimentAnalyzer.predict(embeddings);
  const explanations = explainer.attribute(keywords, intent);
  return { intent, tone, explanations };
}
```

This design meets all constraints: under 15 MB, on-device execution, multilingual support (EN/ES/PT), explainable predictions, and strong privacy controls.

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes end-to-end system design for production NLP under strict latency, privacy, and multilingual requirements, including safeguards against hallucinations.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)
- Hallucination detection and factual verification
- Multilingual adapters and shared encoders
- Privacy constraints and on-device PII prefiltering
- Latency optimization, streaming, drift detection, rollout, and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-pipeline wiring
async function summarizeChat(chat, userLocale) {
  // 1) On-device PII redaction
  const cleanChat = await redactPII(chat);

  // 2) Retrieve relevant context from KB
  const context = await retrieveContext(cleanChat);

  // 3) Generate summary with RAG
  const summary = await generateSummary(cleanChat, context, userLocale);

  // 4) Hallucination detection via cross-check
  const verification = await verifyAgainstKB(summary, context);

  // 5) Confidence gate
  if (verification.confidence < CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD) {
    return { status: 'blocked', reason: 'low_confidence' };
  }

  return { status: 'success', summary: verification.summary };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a real-time, privacy-preserving credibility-verification pipeline with multilingual support and explainability, plus practical KVs like drift handling and rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval-augmented NLP and multilingual inference
- On-device preprocessing and privacy-preserving cloud inference
- Real-time latency budgeting (<250 ms)
- Explainability with citations
- Drift detection, model/versioning, rollback strategy

## Code Example

```javascript
function processMessage(msg) {
  const clean = preprocess(msg);
  const vec = encodeQuery(clean);
  const evidence = retrieveKB(vec);
  const score = scoreCredibility(evidence, msg);
  return explain(evidence, score);
}
```

